+//! c * t1 in the coefficient domain (FIPS 204, Algorithm 8, step 9's c-hat o t1-hat-2^d term,
+//! computed without transforms).
+//!
+//! c has exactly tau = 39 nonzero coefficients, each +1 or -1, so for each row i,
+//! (c * t1_i)[k] = sum over the nonzero c_p of c_p * t1_i[k - p], negacyclically (an index that
+//! wraps below zero takes the opposite sign). All four rows are carried at once: the packed value
+//! T[k] = sum_i t1_i[k] 2^(18 i) holds row i in bits 18i..18i+18, and coefficients k and k + 128
+//! share one felt as X[k] = T[k] + 2^128 T[k + 128]. With Y[k] = T[k + 128] - 2^128 T[k], the
+//! 640-entry buffer F = [-X, -Y, X, Y, -X] makes every shifted copy one contiguous slice: the term
+//! of c_p = +1 is F[256 - p .. 384 - p) and the term of c_p = -1 is F[512 - p .. 640 - p).
+//!
+//! Each output is the sum of 39 slices plus a bias of 2^17 in every 18-bit slot. A slot's sum is
+//! at most 39 * 1023 = 39897 < 2^17 in absolute value, so after the bias every slot lies in
+//! [0, 2^18) and the low and high 128-bit halves of the sum hold coefficients k and k + 128 of
+//! all four rows exactly (the whole sum stays below 2^207, far from the field modulus).
+
+use corelib_imports::bounded_int::{BoundedInt, DivRemHelper, UnitInt, bounded_int, upcast};
