+//! bits 64..128, so theta, chi and iota act on both with the same u128 bitwise operations and pi
+//! only renames words. A rotation by r of both halves is one AND and exact field arithmetic:
+//! with t = w & M_r (the top r bits of each half), t / 2^(64 - r) holds the bits that wrap
+//! around, and rot(w) = w 2^r - (t / 2^(64 - r)) (2^64 - 1), which is below 2^128.
